# Tesseract environment variables — copy this file to .env.local and
# fill in the values. .env.local is gitignored and stays on your machine.
#
# Production / staging values live in Netlify's Environment Variables
# dashboard, not here.

# ─── Supabase (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get these from Supabase dashboard → Settings → API.
# The anon key is safe to commit in client code (it's what your browser
# uses); the service_role key is NOT — it bypasses RLS and must never
# leave Bitwarden or .env.local.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-or-publishable-key

# ─── Sentry error tracking (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# Sentry only initializes when VITE_SENTRY_DSN is set, so local dev stays
# quiet by default. Production and staging set these in Netlify's
# Environment Variables dashboard. The DSN is safe to expose in the
# client bundle (Sentry uses domain allow-lists for security).
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# Logical environment name reported to Sentry — typically "production" or
# "staging". Falls back to Vite's MODE if unset.
VITE_SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=

# ─── Financial data providers ────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are no client-side provider credentials, and there must never be.
#
# This file used to ask for Alpha Vantage and Finnhub keys here. Vite inlines
# every VITE_* variable into the bundle as a string literal, so setting one
# published it: a working Alpha Vantage key was served as plain text in
# dist/assets/index-*.js to anyone who loaded the app. Removed 2026-09-10;
# nothing reads either name any more.
#
# The browser now uses only key-free sources — Yahoo Finance for quotes, with
# Finnhub's published `demo` token behind it. Provider credentials live in
# Supabase function secrets; see the market news section below.
#
# If you find a VITE_* variable elsewhere asking for a provider key, it is a
# mistake, and src/lib/security/__tests__/no-browser-provider-keys.test.ts
# fails on it — in this file as well as in source.

# ─── Financial data layer behavior ───────────────────────────────────────
# The VITE_FINANCIAL_DATA_* knobs documented here are removed. They
# configured src/lib/financial-data/client.ts, which has no importers — the
# ProviderManager half of that module is unreachable from the application, so
# the knobs tuned nothing. See the note in financial-data/config.ts.

# ─── Market news (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by the `market-news` edge function, which merges company news from
# several providers for the Ideas feed. These are set as Supabase *function*
# secrets, not client env vars — they must never reach the browser bundle:
#
#   supabase secrets set FINNHUB_API_KEY=...
#   supabase secrets set ALPHAVANTAGE_API_KEY=...
#
# Each is independently optional. With neither set, the function still
# returns Yahoo Finance results (no key required), so the feed works and
# gets richer as keys are added. Alpha Vantage is the only one of the three
# that supplies sentiment and per-ticker relevance scores.

# ─── Early Access access-request address (optional) ──────────────────────
# Shown as a "Request access" button on /signup during Professional Early
# Access. Leave unset and the page still explains that access is by
# invitation and offers sign-in — it just doesn't render a mailto button.
VITE_ACCESS_REQUEST_EMAIL=
